Z||000006||rockcrawl||01-03-2001||08:16 PM||||Eric,<BR> If you bring it up to my shop I can mount the engine. And if you found a schematic for that Quad 4 (I know you were looking) I can also do the wiring. I personally have done a longitudinal 350TPI Fiero/Lambo, a 3.8 Fiero, a 350TBI S-10, a 460 F-150, a 350CFI CJ5, and a TurboDiesel Wrangler, all without any "kits", so a quad4 would not be a problem (toot-toot on my own horn  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ). I won't be offended if you decline, I really have no professional experience.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Philphine||01-04-2001||02:21 AM||||back home. it's associated auto inc. in hackensack, nj. the kit is $950.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Eric_PA||01-05-2001||07:21 AM||||Thanks for all the info. I have heard the same thing from many about ACE and just wanted to see if I would get the same response on here. Guess what, it looks like I will be staying away from them. <P>Philphine, I did get in touch with Associated Auto last year and talked to Joe W. He told me that in a few months he would have a manual out with the prints to the brackets. I have tried many times to get back in touch with him with no success. I really wanted to go with his kit, but can't ever find him.<P>Rockcrawl, the biggest problem for me is the brackets to mount the engine. I have the trans mounts that bolt right up to the Getrag. As far as the Electrical goes, that's my life. I just can't weld, if I could I would be digging right into it. It would be great if you could help me out with this. I would get another subframe to work with to make things a bit easier. So if your serious about helping me with this maybe sometime you could take a look and let me know how much you would want to do it.<P>Pherder, your car looks great and would love to get a hold of it, but considering I allready have just about everything with the swap I can't swing it. A while back I noticed that you were selling the subframe with the engine and trans mounted. I was really interested until I realized it was on an 88. I know that could be adapted, but am dead set on creating a QUAD powered Fastback just to be different.<P>Thanks,<BR>Eric  <p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 01-05-2001).]||||reg||7
